id: pm-slack-standup-7t31
title: Require exact all-source 100/100/100/100 coverage and strict quality gates
description: "The current V8 coverage gate measures only index.ts at 90.44% lines, 88.23% branches, and 91.79% functions, with no separately reported statements result. release:check now enforces canonical pm-ops ESLint lint and zero-duplication checks plus the docstring gate, but executable scripts remain outside coverage and the mutation and broader static/security gate criteria remain incomplete. This blocks an all-source 100/100/100/100 or production-ready claim."
type: Issue
status: in_progress
priority: 1
tags[4]: coverage,quality-gate,release-blocker,tdd
created_at: "2026-08-21T10:11:53.131Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-04T08:58:55.463Z"
author: codex
estimated_minutes: 720
acceptance_criteria: "Inventory every executable TypeScript and JavaScript source; replace or explicitly justify JavaScript; measure statements, branches, functions, and lines across every executable source at exact 100 percent; make the gate fail when a source is added or removed from measurement; add strict lint, duplication and security/static gates with no blanket suppression; mutation-check the gate; keep tests behavior-driven and non-duplicative"
definition_of_ready: Current release gate and source inventory are measured on main.
reviewer: greptile
risk: high
confidence: high
sprint: 2026-08-quality
release: future
reporter: codex
severity: high
environment: "main 2d0077a, Node V8 coverage"
repro_steps: Run npm run coverage and inspect coverage-gate DEFAULT_SKIP_DIRS plus package thresholds.
expected_result: All executable repository source is measured at exact 100/100/100/100 and every strict quality gate is mandatory.
actual_result: "npm ci and npm run release:check PASS: 207/207 tests, zero skipped; measured index.ts coverage 90.44/88.23/91.79 lines/branches/functions with unchanged 83/87/87 floors; 81 documented declarations. Independent statements, whole-source 100 percent, mutation and broader static/security acceptance remain unmeasured/unaccepted in pm-slack-standup-7t31. Canonical-reader acceptance and all five packed npm/Bun current/minimum/global scenarios pass. Audit all/production zero; strict CI health, pm validate, Bun install and CI fresh-dist comparison pass. Linked packaging tests pass 2/2 and focused PATH fallback test 1/1 passes after failing red on a populated temporary ancestor. The fixture now owns all four searched directories and a shim just outside the bound, preserving real fallback assertions without touching other workspaces. Retained 207 count correction and original 206 history event preserved; all JSONL prefixes unchanged. Note projections support edit/delete in pinned CLI; immutable history is retained. Final-head CI and substantive reviews remain separate; both items released in_progress, never closed."
affected_version: pm-slack-standup 2026.8.17
component: quality and release gates
customer_impact: "A green release gate can coexist with untested source and below-mandate coverage, so it cannot support a production-ready claim."
