  "2026-10-02T21:14:35.906Z",pi-grok,"Current-state actual_result now reports the later 21:38 certification run of 207/207. The 206-test result remains in the append-only history event from 2026-09-28T21:23:29.863Z. Later commits after that run do not add tests."
  "2026-10-03T00:00:48.172Z",codex-sol,"npm ci and npm run release:check PASS: 207/207 tests, zero skipped; measured index.ts coverage 90.44/88.23/91.79 lines/branches/functions with unchanged 83/87/87 floors; 81 documented declarations. Independent statements, whole-source 100 percent, mutation and broader static/security acceptance remain unmeasured/unaccepted in pm-slack-standup-7t31. Canonical-reader acceptance and all five packed npm/Bun current/minimum/global scenarios pass. Audit all/production zero; strict CI health, pm validate, Bun install and CI fresh-dist comparison pass. Linked packaging tests pass 2/2 and focused PATH fallback test 1/1 passes after failing red on a populated temporary ancestor. The fixture now owns all four searched directories and a shim just outside the bound, preserving real fallback assertions without touching other workspaces. Retained 207 count correction and original 206 history event preserved; all JSONL prefixes unchanged. Note projections support edit/delete in pinned CLI; immutable history is retained. Final-head CI and substantive reviews remain separate; both items released in_progress, never closed."
  "2026-10-04T08:50:03.993Z",pi-glm,"cubic-dev-ai finding (PR 97 third round): the description still labeled the superseded 88.38 percent branch figure as current while actual_result reports 88.23. Fixed through the pm CLI in 923e16c: the description's current coverage baseline now states the measured 90.44/88.23/91.79 lines/branches/functions. Historical receipts in the immutable JSONL history are unchanged; the projection edit is appended as a new history event. Full gate re-validated at 923e16c: npm ci and npm run release:check PASS — 207/207 tests, zero skipped; measured index.ts coverage exactly 90.44/88.23/91.79 with unchanged 83/87/87 floors; 81 documented declarations; lint, duplication, canonical-reader, audit:prod, pack, all five packed npm/Bun scenarios, changelog:check, release-changelog-date and publish-attestation green. Independent statements, whole-source 100 percent, mutation and broader static/security acceptance remain unmeasured/unaccepted here."
  "2026-10-04T08:58:54.454Z",pi-glm,"Correction to the previous verification note: the cited 923e16c was amended before it was ever pushed, so it does not resolve in the repository. The coverage-baseline correction and the full release gate evidence are verified at the pushed commit 96d14c3 (npm ci and npm run release:check PASS, 207/207 tests, measured index.ts coverage 90.44/88.23/91.79 with unchanged 83/87/87 floors; linked pm test npm run coverage passes with the same numbers). The original note with the stale reference remains in the immutable history events; this note is the current, verifiable receipt."
notes[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-21T11:48:16.531Z",codex,CodeRabbit exact-head review verified that the description still carried the older 89.66/87.74/90.76 baseline. This append-only update aligns the blocker description with the final measured 89.97/88.32/91.27 result without changing its open status.
  "2026-09-28T21:07:57.383Z",codex,"2026-09-28 certification candidate (pm-slack-standup-74w8): release gate now runs canonical pm-ops lint, duplication and docstring checks, but V8 coverage still reports only index.ts at 90.44% lines, 88.38% branches, 91.79% functions; no independently reported statements dimension or whole-source coverage. This open item remains the readiness blocker. The package upgrade PR does not claim 100/100/100/100."
